## What I produced
**`courses/.../lessons/adnotacja-i-konwersja-z-cocopascal-voc.json`** — module `m3`, 14 min, Polish prose (English technical terms kept per the course's research note). It passes `LessonSchema.safeParse` (confirmed via vitest with the project's `@/` alias — the SKILL's bare `tsx` snippet can't resolve that alias, so I validated through vitest instead).
**Structure** — 2 theory beats + 5 widgets, no two theories back-to-back, ends on a widget:
1. **theory** — annotation tools + the three coordinate conventions, with an inline 3-panel figure; carries section-level VOC + COCO paper sources.
2. **dataTable** — COCO vs VOC vs YOLO cheat-sheet (convention / units / normalized / file type).
3. **quiz** — the #1 dataset misconception (pixels vs normalized, corners vs center); distractors are the VOC and COCO conventions verbatim.
4. **theory** — the conversion math in KaTeX (VOC→YOLO and COCO→YOLO) + a worked numeric example figure + the two real-world pitfalls; section sources point at the Ultralytics COCO→YOLO docs and JSON2YOLO.
5. **code** — implement `voc_to_yolo(box, img_w, img_h)`; 4 tests (1 visible smoke test + 3 hidden), full reference `solution`. I ran the solution against all four test bodies — they pass.
6. **dragMatch** — match each format to its box convention.
7. **sandbox** — convert a small vehicle/ship VOC mini-set to YOLO `.txt` lines.
**Assets** — two matplotlib figures generated and saved under `assets/images/` (`box-trzy-formaty.png`, `voc-do-yolo-przyklad.png`), both referenced via local `/api/courses/.../assets/images/...` paths. `grep` confirms zero external `http(s)` image URLs.
**Sources** — 5 lesson-level entries (3 articles + 2 papers; both papers carry author + year), all stable hosts.
Untouched: `course.json`, other lessons, `research.md`, `sources.md`, and `scripts/ralph/` (all clean). No stray temp files left behind.
